## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design dynamic, policy-driven routing with on-edge latency constraints, multi-tenant safeguards, and auditable provenance. It also probes risk scoring, drift detection, and rollback semantics under real-world operational pressures.

## Key Concepts

- Contextual bandits for real-time routing decisions
- Per-tenant safety profiles and data locality constraints
- Latency budgets and SLA adherence (p95 targets)
- Drift detection and automated rollback to baseline
- Tamper-evident, cryptographically signed per-tenant audit logs

## Code Example

```javascript
function selectVariant(context, stats) {
  // context: {tenant, latency, safetyProfile}
  // stats: {risk, base, tuned, safety}
  if (Math.random() < 0.1) return 'base';
  if (stats.risk > 0.6) return 'safety-guarded';
  const scores = { base: stats.base, tuned: stats.tuned, safety: stats.safety };
  return Object.keys(scores).reduce((a,b) => scores[a] > scores[b] ? a : b);
}
```

